Phase 1 – SQL to PySpark

Learned:

Basic PySpark DataFrame operations
Mapping SQL queries to PySpark syntax
Using select, filter, and groupBy
Understanding how data is stored and processed in DataFrames
Writing simple transformations and actions (show, count)
Difference between SQL queries and PySpark DataFrame API
How to load and explore data using .show() and .printSchema()
Applying conditions using filter() and logical operators

Challenges:

Understanding how groupBy works compared to SQL
Getting comfortable with syntax differences between SQL and PySpark
Remembering function-based syntax instead of SQL keywords
Handling errors due to incorrect column references
Confusion between DataFrame operations and SQL queries
Writing conditions using & and | instead of AND / OR
Understanding how transformations are executed in PySpark